WEBVTT

00:16:27.435 --> 00:16:32.087
is it almost sounds like
it's a weak culture,

00:16:32.111 --> 00:16:36.509
that it's kind of dispersed
and there's not anything consistent

00:16:36.533 --> 00:16:38.479
or strong about it.

00:16:38.503 --> 00:16:40.794
And that to me is a big part

00:16:40.818 --> 00:16:43.399
of the difference between
weak and strong cultures.

00:16:43.423 --> 00:16:47.176
So in my world we normally
define a weak culture as existing

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:49.149
when you go around to different people

00:16:49.173 --> 00:16:50.694
and you ask what the values are

00:16:50.718 --> 00:16:52.512
and they all name different values,

00:16:52.536 --> 00:16:54.778
and nobody really cares about them.

00:16:54.802 --> 00:16:57.390
In a strong culture,
the values are widely shared,

00:16:57.414 --> 00:17:00.225
so everybody believes
the values are the same.